 definitiva de la mujer en el rock (Terry Garthwaite, Joan Armatrading, Nanci Griffith y, sobre todo, Rickie Lee Jones, protegida de Tom Waits); la escuela tejana de cantautores herederos de Townes Van Zandt (Guy Clark, Butch Hancock, Joe Ely, Terry Allen, Rodney Crowell, T-Bone Burnett); el populismo melancólico de la posguerra de Vietnam (Warren Zevon, Rick Danko, Steve Forbert, John Hiatt, John Mellencamp, Don Henley, Donald Fagen, Robbie Robertson); y el puente de 1977 hacia la new wave: Peter Gabriel, poeta atormentado de las neurosis postindustriales, Marianne Faithfull y Kate Bush.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#auteurs"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":88822489008573,"artist":"Bryan Adams","artist_id":113205708501383,"title":"Straight From The Heart","year":1983,"ess":0,"yt":"ImCTOtOJyi0","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Los autores (1975-1990)","scene_id":77707013048741,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#auteurs","chapters":["Sección 4.6"],"pages":[[1,97,null]]},{"id":98618229355020,"artist":"Bryan Adams","artist_id":113205708501383,"title":"Run To You","year":1984,"ess":0,"yt":"nCBASt507WA","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Los autores (1975-1990)","scene_id":77707013048741,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#auteurs","chapters":["Sección 4.6"],"pages":[[1,97,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":97,"text":"…Of Love (1985), each packed with a hurricane of quasi-jazz saxophones, blues harmonica, boogie guitars and gospel organs. On the commercial front, Bryan Adams split his career between heartfelt torch ballads (Straight From The Heart, 1983) and lush, riff-driven rockers (Run To You, 1984). Robbie Robertson…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Elevating Canadian Production (1980s)","body":"Bryan Adams was cited by Gino Vannelli as an artist who, in the 1980s, contributed to elevating Canadian record production to \"world-class\" standards, allowing artists to manage their careers from Canada rather than needing to move to the United States. \"he cited Celine Dion and Brian Adams as artists that elevated the production of records. And when he said that they became world class, what he meant was that you didn't have to go to the United States to have your career. You could orchestrate your career from Canada.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 45 - Oh, Canada! Canada's Rock Music Industry in the 70s","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 45 - Oh, Canada! Canada's Rock Music Industry in the 70s","url":"https://www.ftr70.com/"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Emergence as Serious Stars","body":"Bryan Adams emerged as one of the serious stars through the late 1970s and into the 1980s, benefiting from the new industry infrastructure and increased radio support for Canadian talent. This period marked a shift towards greater national and international success for homegrown artists. \"Love her boy, Chilla Wack, Bruce Coburn, rough trade, the pay-all was Toronto, the headpins, the spoons, bride-adams, parachute club, men without hats, Cory Hart. They all emerged as serious stars through the late 1970s and into the 1980s.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Roots of the 90s CanRock Explosion","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6PGgNCaW4xo"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Mid-1980s Domestic & International Success","body":"By the mid-1980s, Bryan Adams was among several Canadian rock acts that released albums performing \"extremely well domestically and internationally,\" some even achieving multi-platinum sales in foreign markets. \"Rush, April Wine, BTO, Loverboy, Triumph, Brian Adams, and a half a dozen others all released albums that had done extremely well domestically and internationally.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 8: The CanRock Revolution","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U2kYleeMnl8"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Photography Hobby","body":"Brian Adams is engaged in photography as a personal interest. \"Brian Adams is into photography.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Kirk Hammett’s Movie Poster Collection ｜ Bonus Podcast","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CgDCaUxbQDU"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Jack Richardson Producer of the Year Award (1984)","body":"Nominated.","year":1984,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6114830"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Juno Award for Album of the Year (1984) — Cuts Like a Knife","body":"Nominated.","year":1984,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6314042"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Juno Award for Single of the Year (1984)","body":"Nominated.","year":1984,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6314103"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Juno Award for Songwriter of the Year (1984) — Cuts Like a Knife","body":"Nominated.","year":1984,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6314105"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Juno Award for Songwriter of the Year (1984) — Straight from the Heart","body":"Nominated.","year":1984,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6314105"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best Male Rock Vocal Performance (1985) — Reckless","body":"Nominated.","year":1985,"extra":null,"srcs":[