e friends with members of Death Cab for Cutie.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Tegan and Sarah","from_id":184924432787248,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Driven By Her: Women of the 21st Century","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=11UsTJQyQds"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Location and Building History","body":"The Warehouse Studio is situated in the Gastown area of Vancouver, operating out of the city's oldest brick building. Built in 1886 as a grocery warehouse, it later served as Vancouver City Hall, then reverted to a glass company warehouse. After falling into disuse and suffering fires, Bryan Adams purchased and extensively restored the almost completely burned-out building in 1991. \"It was built, yes, as a warehouse, a grocery warehouse in 1886.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Florence + the Machine","from_id":29163890797074,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Legendary Recording Studios","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N5kSZOl-5UY"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Success and Artist Retreat","body":"Le Studio achieved great success, allowing artists to \"cocoon themselves\" for extended periods to complete their projects. Its client list included renowned acts such as Rush, The Police, Sting, The Bee Gees, David Bowie, and Bryan Adams. \"La Studio was fantastically successful.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Florence + the Machine","from_id":29163890797074,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Legendary Recording Studios","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N5kSZOl-5UY"}]}],"charts":[{"id":88822489008573,"type":"song","name":"Straight from the Heart","work_year":1983,"list_id":120682792121633,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1983","src":"singles","rank":71,"year":1983,"note":"","yt":"ImCTOtOJyi0","scaruffi":null},{"id":88822489008573,"type":"song","name":"Straight from the Heart","work_year":1983,"list_id":13233582